# Storage by team and bucket

The hierarchy is a field, not nested data: `parent` names a column, and the
three team rows are never written because a parent cell that names no row of its
own creates the group anyway. Each branch takes one hue and every tile under it
wears the same one, so a reader tracks a team by colour and reads its
subdivision from the gaps.

```mdv treemap
title: Object storage (TB)
category: bucket
value: tb
parent: team
tile: squarify
labelMinArea: 900
format: table
---
bucket          | team      |   tb
media-originals | Platform  | 41.2
media-derived   | Platform  | 18.7
build-cache     | Platform  |  9.4
event-archive   | Analytics | 33.8
warehouse-cold  | Analytics | 22.1
notebooks       | Analytics |  4.6
session-replays | Product   | 15.3
exports         | Product   |  6.9
attachments     | Product   |  3.2
```
